    Block {
      BlockType		      SubSystem
      Name		      "KINARM_HandFeedbackInTarget"
      SID		      "5"
      Ports		      [1, 1]
      Position		      [165, 564, 295, 626]
      ZOrder		      -4
      BackgroundColor	      "green"
      AncestorBlock	      "KINARM_general/KINARM_HandInTarget"
      LibraryVersion	      "*"
      MinAlgLoopOccurrences   off
      PropExecContextOutsideSubsystem off
      RTWSystemCode	      "Auto"
      FunctionWithSeparateData off
      Opaque		      off
      RequestExecContextInheritance off
      MaskHideContents	      off
      Object {
	$PropName		"MaskObject"
	$ObjectID		19
	$ClassName		"Simulink.Mask"
	Type			"KINARM_HandInTarget"
	Description		"This block returns a vector or array corresponding to the Target_Table rows indicating whether the spec"
	"ified hand is in (=1) or out (=0) of each of the targets.\n"
	Help			"Used to determine if the hand (finger-tip) is in any of the targets in the Target_Table.\n<P>\n<B><I>Use of t"
	"his block requires that the DataLogging block (General library) be set to log KINARM data.</I></B>\n\n<H2>Library </H"
	"2>\nKINARM_general (sub-library)\n\n<H2>Description </H2>\nThis block returns a vector or array corresponding to the "
	"Target_Table rows indicating whether the specified hand (i.e. finger-tip) is in or out of each of the targets.  Each "
	"element in the output vector or output array will be either a 0 (hand not in target) or a 1 (hand in target).\n<P> \n"
	"A vector is returned if only one target state is specified in each target row (see Parameters and Dialog Box), with e"
	"ach index of the vector corresponding to a row in the target table.  An array is returned if more than one target sta"
	"te is specified in a target row, with each row of the array corresponding to a target row and each column correspondi"
	"ng to the nth target state specified in each target row.  \n<P>\nThe output vector or array is typically used by a st"
	"ateflow chart to affect behavior of the system.  Because this block returns hand-in-target information for all target"
	"s in the target table, multiple targets can be monitored at once (i.e. the stateflow chart could have certain transit"
	"ions that occur if the hand is in one target and other transitions if it is in a different target).  Likewise, becaus"
	"e this block returns hand-in-target information for multiple states of a single target, those multiple states can be "
	"monitored simultaneously.\n<P> \nBecause the KINARM_HandInTarget block returns information for only one hand, two cop"
	"ies of this block are required if information for both hands is desired.\n<P>\n\n<H2>Parameters and Dialog Box</H2>\n"
	"<B>Dominant Hand?:</B> this box determines which hand is used by this block : dominant hand position (checked box) or"
	" the non-dominant hand position (unchecked box).  (Note: if the end-user wants to know about both the dominant hand a"
	"nd the non-dominant hand, then 2 separate copies of this block are requried, one for each hand.)\n<P>\n<B>Type of Tar"
	"get:</B> Enter the type of target specified in the target table:   \n<P>\n<B>Number of Target States:</B> Enter the n"
	"umber of target states specified in each target row.  Up to four target states are allowed per target row.\n<P>\n<B>S"
	"tate <n> Target Table Columns:</B> Enter the columns in the Target Table that specify the relevant target attributes."
	"  Do this for each target state.\nFor a circle, enter the columns corresponding to logical radius (e.g. 4)\n<BR>For a"
	"n ellipse, enter the columns corresponding to major radius, minor radius, rotation angle (e.g. [4, 5, 6]).\n<BR>For a"
	" rectangle, enter the columns corresponding to length, height, and rotation angle (e.g. [4, 5, 6]).\n<BR>For a line, "
	"enter the columns corresponding to stroke width, endpoint in x, and endpoint in y (e.g. [3, 4, 5]).\n<BR>For a triang"
	"le, enter the columns corresponding to length, height, peak offset, and rotation angle (e.g. [4, 5, 6, 7]).\n\n<H2>Ex"
	"amples</H2>\n<B>Example 1.</B>  Suppose a target row will be used to define 1 state for a circle type target and the "
	"radius of the visual target is the same radius to be used for determination of hand-in-target.  The related Target Ta"
	"ble column is: column 6 = radius.  For this example, \"State 1 Target Table Columns\" would equal [6].\n<P> \n\n<B>Ex"
	"ample 2.</B>  Suppose a target row will be used to define 1 state for a circle type target, but the radius of the vis"
	"ual target will be different than the radius to be used for determination of hand-in-target.  This option allows inde"
	"pendent control over the size of the visual target versus the accuracy needed to be considered \"in the target\".  Th"
	"e related Target Table columns are: column 6 = radius1 (i.e. radius to target to be drawn); column 7 = radius2 (i.e. "
	"radius to be used for hand-in-target) .  For this example, \"State 1 Target Table Columns\" would equal [7].\n<P>\n<B"
	">Example 3.</B>  Suppose a target row will be used to define 2 states for a circle type target, where the radius of t"
	"he visual target will be a constant, but depending on the state of the system, one of 2 other and different radii wil"
	"l be used for determination of hand-in-target.  The related Target Table columns are: column 6 = radius1 (i.e. radius"
	" to target to be drawn); column 7 = radius2 (i.e. radius to be used for hand-in-target for state 1); column 8 = radiu"
	"s3 (i.e. radius to be used for hand-in-target for state 2).  For this example, \"State 1 Target Table Columns\" would"
	" equal [7], while \"State 2 Target Table Columns\" would equal [8].\n<P>\n\n<H2>Related Blocks </H2>\nDataLogging"
	Initialization		"num_states=str2num(get_param(gcb, 'num_states'));\ncolumntext='(columns: ';\n\nfor i=1:num_states\n	"
	"varname=['attribcol' num2str(i)];\n	if i>1\n		columntext=[columntext, '; '];\n	end\n	columntext=[columntext, get_para"
	"m(gcb, varname)];\nend\ncolumntext=strvcat([columntext ')'],' ', ' ');\n\noutput_block=char(find_system(gcb,'LookUnde"
	"rMasks','all','FollowLinks','on','SearchDepth',1,'BlockType','Outport'));\noutputname=get_param(output_block,'Name');"
	"\n\n% Select only the desired states for output. The output port is also renamed to reflect \n% whether the output is"
	" a vector (in the case of a single state) or an array (of vectors, \n% one for each of multiple states).\nif num_stat"
	"es == 1\n	set_param([gcb '/Selected States'], 'Value', '[1]');\n	set_param(output_block, 'Name', 'HandInTarget_Vector"
	"');\nelseif num_states == 2\n	set_param([gcb '/Selected States'], 'Value', '[1,2]');\n	set_param(output_block, 'Name'"
	", 'HandInTarget_Array');\nelseif num_states == 3\n	set_param([gcb '/Selected States'], 'Value', '[1,2,3]');\n	set_par"
	"am(output_block, 'Name', 'HandInTarget_Array');\nelse\n	set_param([gcb '/Selected States'], 'Value', '[1,2,3,4]');\n	"
	"set_param(output_block, 'Name', 'HandInTarget_Array');\nend\n\n"
	SelfModifiable		"on"
	Display			"disp(columntext)\nport_label('output',1,outputname)\n"
	Array {
	  Type			  "Simulink.MaskParameter"
	  Dimension		  7
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    20
	    Type		    "checkbox"
	    Name		    "use_dominant_hand"
	    Prompt		    "Dominant Hand?"
	    Value		    "on"
	  }
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    21
	    Type		    "popup"
	    Array {
	      Type		      "Cell"
	      Dimension		      5
	      Cell		      "Circle"
	      Cell		      "Ellipse"
	      Cell		      "Rectangle"
	      Cell		      "Line"
	      Cell		      "Triangle"
	      PropName		      "TypeOptions"
	    }
	    Name		    "target_type"
	    Prompt		    "Type of Target"
	    Value		    "Circle"
	    Callback		    "target_type=get_param(gcb, 'target_type');\nattribcol1=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol1')) 0 0 "
	    "0 0 0 0];\nattribcol2=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol2')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol3=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'a"
	    "ttribcol3')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol4=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol4')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nswitch target_type(1"
	    ":3)\n	case 'Cir'\n		numcol=1;\n	case 'Ell'\n		numcol=3;\n    case 'Rec'\n        numcol=3;\n    case 'Lin'\n     "
	    "   numcol=3;\n    case 'Tri'\n        numcol=4;\n	otherwise\n		numcol=1;\nend\nif numcol==1\n	set_param(gcb, 'att"
	    "ribcol1', num2str(attribcol1(1)));\n	set_param(gcb, 'attribcol2', num2str(attribcol2(1)));\n	set_param(gcb, 'attr"
	    "ibcol3', num2str(attribcol3(1)));\n	set_param(gcb, 'attribcol4', num2str(attribcol4(1)));\nelse\n	set_param(gcb, "
	    "'attribcol1', ['[' num2str(attribcol1(1:numcol)) ']']);\n	set_param(gcb, 'attribcol2', ['[' num2str(attribcol2(1:"
	    "numcol)) ']']);\n	set_param(gcb, 'attribcol3', ['[' num2str(attribcol3(1:numcol)) ']']);\n	set_param(gcb, 'attrib"
	    "col4', ['[' num2str(attribcol4(1:numcol)) ']']);\nend"
	  }
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    22
	    Type		    "popup"
	    Array {
	      Type		      "Cell"
	      Dimension		      4
	      Cell		      "1"
	      Cell		      "2"
	      Cell		      "3"
	      Cell		      "4"
	      PropName		      "TypeOptions"
	    }
	    Name		    "num_states"
	    Prompt		    "Number of Target States"
	    Value		    "1"
	    Callback		    "num_states = str2num(get_param(gcb, 'num_states'));\nvis = get_param(gcb, 'MaskVisibilities');\n\n"
	    "% Select only the desired states for output. The output port is also renamed to reflect \n% whether the output is"
	    " a vector (in the case of a single state) or an array (of vectors, \n% one for each of multiple states).\noutput_"
	    "block=char(find_system(gcb, 'LookUnderMasks', 'all', 'FollowLinks', 'on', 'SearchDepth', 1, 'BlockType', 'Outport"
	    "'));\n\nif num_states == 1\n	set_param([gcb '/Selected States'], 'Value', '[1]');\n	set_param(output_block, 'Name"
	    "', 'HandInTarget_Vector');\n	vis{5} = 'off';\n	vis{6} = 'off';\n	vis{7} = 'off';\nelseif num_states == 2\n	set_pa"
	    "ram([gcb '/Selected States'], 'Value', '[1,2]');\n	set_param(output_block, 'Name', 'HandInTarget_Array');\n	vis{5"
	    "} = 'on';\n	vis{6} = 'off';\n	vis{7} = 'off';\nelseif num_states == 3\n	set_param([gcb '/Selected States'], 'Valu"
	    "e', '[1,2,3]');\n	set_param(output_block, 'Name','HandInTarget_Array');\n	vis{5} = 'on';\n	vis{6} = 'on';\n	vis{7"
	    "} = 'off';\nelse\n	set_param([gcb '/Selected States'], 'Value', '[1,2,3,4]');\n	set_param(output_block, 'Name', '"
	    "HandInTarget_Array');\n	vis{5} = 'on';\n	vis{6} = 'on';\n	vis{7} = 'on';\nend\nset_param(gcb, 'MaskVisibilities',"
	    " vis);\n\ntarget_type=get_param(gcb, 'target_type');\nattribcol1=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol1')) 0 0 0 0 0"
	    " 0];\nattribcol2=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol2')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol3=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attrib"
	    "col3')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol4=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol4')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nswitch target_type(1:3)\n"
	    "	case 'Cir'\n		numcol=1;\n	case 'Ell'\n		numcol=3;\n    case 'Rec'\n        numcol=3;\n    case 'Lin'\n        nu"
	    "mcol=3;\n    case 'Tri'\n        numcol=4;\n	otherwise\n		numcol=1;\nend\nif numcol==1\n	set_param(gcb, 'attribco"
	    "l1', num2str(attribcol1(1)));\n	set_param(gcb, 'attribcol2', num2str(attribcol2(1)));\n	set_param(gcb, 'attribcol"
	    "3', num2str(attribcol3(1)));\n	set_param(gcb, 'attribcol4', num2str(attribcol4(1)));\nelse\n	set_param(gcb, 'attr"
	    "ibcol1', ['[' num2str(attribcol1(1:numcol)) ']']);\n	set_param(gcb, 'attribcol2', ['[' num2str(attribcol2(1:numco"
	    "l)) ']']);\n	set_param(gcb, 'attribcol3', ['[' num2str(attribcol3(1:numcol)) ']']);\n	set_param(gcb, 'attribcol4'"
	    ", ['[' num2str(attribcol4(1:numcol)) ']']);\nend\n"
	  }
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    23
	    Type		    "edit"
	    Name		    "attribcol1"
	    Prompt		    "State 1 Target Table Column(s)"
	    Value		    "4"
	    Callback		    "target_type=get_param(gcb, 'target_type');\nattribcol1=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol1')) 0 0 "
	    "0 0 0 0];\nattribcol2=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol2')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol3=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'a"
	    "ttribcol3')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nattribcol4=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'attribcol4')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nswitch target_type(1"
	    ":3)\n	case 'Cir'\n		numcol=1;\n	case 'Ell'\n		numcol=3;\n    case 'Rec'\n        numcol=3;\n    case 'Lin'\n     "
	    "   numcol=3;\n    case 'Tri'\n        numcol=4;\n	otherwise\n		numcol=1;\nend\nif numcol==1\n	set_param(gcb, 'att"
	    "ribcol1', num2str(attribcol1(1)));\n	set_param(gcb, 'attribcol2', num2str(attribcol2(1)));\n	set_param(gcb, 'attr"
	    "ibcol3', num2str(attribcol3(1)));\n	set_param(gcb, 'attribcol4', num2str(attribcol4(1)));\nelse\n	set_param(gcb, "
	    "'attribcol1', ['[' num2str(attribcol1(1:numcol)) ']']);\n	set_param(gcb, 'attribcol2', ['[' num2str(attribcol2(1:"
